# Captured warehouse-lineage payloads (#858 spike, 2026-07-17). Redacted at capture
# time (usernames pseudonymized), parked here for the fixture-backed tests.
#
# Only the payloads a committed test actually reads are checked in — each after a
# per-file review for sensitive content (the #823 lesson: tests ride REAL payloads,
# but a real payload still gets read before it is committed). Everything else stays
# local until the slice that needs it lands.
*
!.gitignore
!snowflake_object_dependencies.json
!uc_table_lineage_projected.json
# #901 column grain — reviewed 2026-07-18: table/column names + event times only.
!uc_column_lineage_projected.json
# #908 Enterprise ACCESS_HISTORY columns — reviewed 2026-07-18: table/column names
# only (incl. quoted-lowercase workout tables — real identity shapes); every
# directSources is empty (the whole point of the fixture: no fabrication).
!sf_access_history_columns_projected.json
# #919 inventory enumeration — reviewed 2026-07-28: catalog/schema/table identifiers
# only (SF INFORMATION_SCHEMA.TABLES account-wide capture incl. SNOWFLAKE system db;
# UC system.information_schema capture incl. samples + information_schema rows —
# the noise the enumerator's scope predicates exist to exclude).
!snowflake_tables_casing.json
!uc_tables_casing.json
# #892 GET_LINEAGE traversal (live prod Enterprise capture) — reviewed 2026-07-28:
# catalog identifiers + object domains/statuses only, three `SELECT *` results kept
# verbatim (incl. the capture harness's `str()` of NULLs as the literal "None" — the
# loader maps them back). Contains one MASKED row whose name parts are `***` (the
# whole point of the fixture: a redacted endpoint must never become an asset) and one
# `process` blob carrying a Snowflake `query_id` — an opaque execution identifier, no
# SQL text, no data values, no principal names.
!sf_get_lineage_projected.json
# #912 Snowpark-scratch stitch (365d ACCESS_HISTORY capture) — reviewed 2026-07-28:
# six rows, table names + column names/ids only. Every `directSources` is empty (these
# are COPY-from-stage writes), and three rows have a NULL source (a stage upload with
# no table-lineage source at all) — both are real shapes the parser must survive.
!sf_access_history_snowpark_projected.json
